       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 4,250 mg three times daily, which is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day in the US (2,000\u20133,000 mg/day elsewhere). The usual maximum for a single dose is 1,000 mg, and 850 mg is the largest standard tablet strength.\n- **Risk:** This is about 5 times the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended doses include:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **425 mg three times daily:** not a standard strength, so probably not what you meant.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** at a different frequency.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency. Once you do, I'll enter it right away. Also check the dose with your resident or pharmacist before it's signed. If you really do want 4,250 mg, tell me the clinical reason and I'll flag it in the order note. I'd still advise confirming with your supervising physician first."
